WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.489 --> 00:00:17.010
Jason walked into Kids Central and sat down between Bobby and Nina.

2
00:00:19.031 --> 00:00:23.153
"Ah-choo!" Jason held a tissue to his nose.

3
00:00:23.173 --> 00:00:26.134
"Do you have a cold, Jason?"

4
00:00:26.414 --> 00:00:27.355
Miss Shelly asked.

5
00:00:27.375 --> 00:00:29.936
"No." Jason shrugged.

6
00:00:30.552 --> 00:00:32.453
"But sometimes cats make me sneeze."

7
00:00:32.473 --> 00:00:35.054
"There are no cats in here!"

8
00:00:35.374 --> 00:00:36.094
Bobby said.

9
00:00:36.114 --> 00:00:37.435
"Just people."

10
00:00:37.455 --> 00:00:40.916
"Ah-choo!" Jason sneezed again.

11
00:00:42.037 --> 00:00:43.637
Nina handed him another tissue.

12
00:00:43.657 --> 00:00:49.580
"We're playing a game called twenty questions today," Miss Shelly said.

13
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.261
"Jason, do you want to be 'it'?"

14
00:00:53.562 --> 00:00:56.343
"Sure." Jason nodded, and blew his nose.

15
00:00:56.363 --> 00:00:59.324
"Good," Miss Shelly said.

16
00:00:59.864 --> 00:01:02.285
"Think of a person, place, or thing.

17
00:01:03.286 --> 00:01:05.567
Everyone else will try to guess what it is."

18
00:01:05.587 --> 00:01:08.288
"Hmm," Jason thought.

19
00:01:09.508 --> 00:01:11.029
"I could choose a person."

20
00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:12.710
He thought of Ms.

21
00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:14.451
Folani and George Washington.

22
00:01:15.111 --> 00:01:16.391
But they seemed too easy.

23
00:01:16.411 --> 00:01:21.034
"Maybe I'll choose a place like Africa or Pauly's Pizza.

24
00:01:21.674 --> 00:01:23.975
Or He sneezed loudly.

25
00:01:23.995 --> 00:01:26.236
"Okay, I'm ready."

26
00:01:27.732 --> 00:01:29.833
Miss Shelly nodded and looked at the other kids.

27
00:01:29.853 --> 00:01:33.494
"Jason is thinking of a person, place, or thing.

28
00:01:34.354 --> 00:01:37.115
You can ask him yes or no questions about it."

29
00:01:37.135 --> 00:01:41.356
"We can only ask twenty questions, right?"

30
00:01:41.716 --> 00:01:42.396
Izzie asked.

31
00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:46.137
"Right!" Miss Shelly said with a smile.

32
00:01:47.337 --> 00:01:49.378
She handed Nina some paper and a pencil.

33
00:01:49.398 --> 00:01:53.219
"Nina will record how many questions you ask."

34
00:01:54.519 --> 00:01:55.500
"I'm first!"

35
00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:56.520
Bobby said.

36
00:01:57.152 --> 00:02:00.295
"Jason, is it a person, a place, or a thing?"

37
00:02:00.315 --> 00:02:04.438
"You can't ask that, Bobby," Izzie said.

38
00:02:04.458 --> 00:02:08.821
"Jason can only answer yes or no questions."

39
00:02:08.841 --> 00:02:10.983
"Oh yeah."

40
00:02:11.223 --> 00:02:12.264
Bobby tried again.

41
00:02:12.284 --> 00:02:13.925
"Is it a person?"

42
00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:17.048
"No," Jason said.

43
00:02:17.068 --> 00:02:20.251
"Is it a thing?"

44
00:02:20.671 --> 00:02:21.391
Izzie asked.

45
00:02:21.411 --> 00:02:24.074
"Ah-choo! No."

46
00:02:24.094 --> 00:02:27.816
"Two questions so far," Nina said.

47
00:02:27.836 --> 00:02:31.238
"So it's a place," Ethan said.

48
00:02:31.258 --> 00:02:33.960
"Is it in Pennsylvania?"

49
00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:38.722
"Yes." "Is it in our town?"

50
00:02:39.083 --> 00:02:39.843
Nina asked.

51
00:02:39.863 --> 00:02:44.526
"Yes." "Is it outside?"

52
00:02:44.866 --> 00:02:45.566
Bobby asked.

53
00:02:45.586 --> 00:02:47.707
"Ah-choo! Nope."

54
00:02:48.888 --> 00:02:51.589
"Hmm." Izzie tapped her chin.

55
00:02:52.990 --> 00:02:54.651
"Have we all been there?"

56
00:02:54.671 --> 00:02:58.056
"Yes." Ethan was next.

57
00:02:58.076 --> 00:03:01.217
"Do we like to go there?"

58
00:03:01.237 --> 00:03:06.219
"Yes." "Does the place have tables?"

59
00:03:06.639 --> 00:03:07.419
Nina asked.

60
00:03:08.879 --> 00:03:10.660
"Yes," Jason said.

61
00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:13.440
Nina looked at her sheet of paper.

62
00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:15.821
"That's eight questions.

63
00:03:16.621 --> 00:03:18.202
We have twelve more left."

64
00:03:18.222 --> 00:03:20.202
"I know!"

65
00:03:20.582 --> 00:03:21.403
Bobby cried.

66
00:03:21.423 --> 00:03:23.583
"Is it Kids Central?"

67
00:03:24.623 --> 00:03:26.144
"No," said Jason.

68
00:03:26.848 --> 00:03:28.009
Bobby looked grumpy.

69
00:03:29.949 --> 00:03:31.510
"Is the place at school?"

70
00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:32.610
asked Izzie.

71
00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:34.431
"Yes! Ah-choo!"

72
00:03:35.932 --> 00:03:37.612
Ethan's stomach growled.

73
00:03:37.652 --> 00:03:39.713
"Is it the cafeteria?"

74
00:03:39.733 --> 00:03:42.634
"Yes!" Jason said.

75
00:03:42.654 --> 00:03:46.756
"Ethan guessed correctly," Miss Shelly said.

76
00:03:46.776 --> 00:03:49.357
"So he gets to be 'it' next."

77
00:03:49.377 --> 00:03:54.059
"I have to sharpen this pencil," Nina said.

78
00:03:54.819 --> 00:03:56.560
She got up to get her pencil sharpener.

79
00:03:59.868 --> 00:04:02.069
As she opened her backpack, she gasped.

80
00:04:02.089 --> 00:04:04.611
"Oh no!

81
00:04:05.131 --> 00:04:06.392
Guess what I found!"

82
00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:09.113
"Ah-choo! Ah-choo!"

83
00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:12.235
"Does it make Jason sneeze?"

84
00:04:12.695 --> 00:04:13.435
Izzie asked.

85
00:04:13.455 --> 00:04:15.656
"Yes!" Nina said.

86
00:04:15.676 --> 00:04:18.518
"Is it fuzzy?"

87
00:04:18.818 --> 00:04:19.539
Ethan said.

88
00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:22.040
"Yes!" said Nina.

89
00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:26.202
"Ah-choo!" "Is it a cat?"

90
00:04:26.502 --> 00:04:27.323
Bobby asked.

91
00:04:27.343 --> 00:04:29.504
"No," Nina said.

92
00:04:30.332 --> 00:04:32.453
"But it belongs to a cat."

93
00:04:32.473 --> 00:04:36.035
"Let's see, Nina," Miss Shelly said.

94
00:04:36.916 --> 00:04:38.737
Nina pulled something from her backpack.

95
00:04:38.757 --> 00:04:42.019
"Ah-choo! Ah-choo!"

96
00:04:42.539 --> 00:04:44.200
Jason sneezed and sneezed.

97
00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:48.102
"It's my cat's brush," Nina said.

98
00:04:48.122 --> 00:04:52.585
"Let's get it outside quickly," Miss Shelly said.

99
00:04:53.645 --> 00:04:55.626
Nina hurried to put the brush outside.

100
00:04:57.147 --> 00:04:58.568
Then she ran over to Jason.

101
00:04:59.752 --> 00:05:01.313
"I'm so sorry, Jason!"

102
00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:03.135
He blew his nose.

103
00:05:03.155 --> 00:05:05.576
"I'm glad you found it.

104
00:05:06.497 --> 00:05:08.899
Otherwise I could have sneezed all afternoon!"
